<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose five points to 1,269.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose five points to 1,269.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,269 today from 1,264 on May 6, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1353    12.288	  1354    12.293</p>
<p>   1a   1249  9463.000	  1241  9400.000</p>
<p>   2    1527    21.813	  1522    21.750</p>
<p>   2a   1498 12288.000	  1481 12143.000</p>
<p>   3    1368    12.619	  1365    12.593</p>
<p>   3a   1150  9075.000	  1140  9000.000</p>
<p>   6    1228    12.669	  1231    12.693</p>
<p>   7    1153     5.613	  1153     5.614</p>
<p>   8     882     9.700	   884     9.721</p>
<p>   9     704  6156.000	   697  6093.000</p>
<p>  10    1112     5.619	  1111     5.614</p>
